{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KXTMZ9EuJggQfo5svjN8QB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Cheetah 未能干净复现 CIVO 模式（NVE 停留在 0.8-1.4x，无加速性过估计签名），Cartpole/ManiSkill3 亦无清晰 CIVO 信号。\n  论文退守为 Walker Walk 单环境深度机制研究。核心贡献重新定位为：\n  (1) 首个严格析因诊断——在 DreamerV3 imagination-based actor-critic 中揭示 temporal abstraction 失败的 specific causal chain；\n  (2) NVE 诊断方法论（Walker 内 4/4 完美分类，提议更广泛使用但承认跨环境泛化受限）；\n  (3) gradient-level 因果证据（Full-SGS NVE 1.00x）证明失败是 observation-decoder-driven 而非 reward-driven——即便限于单环境亦非显然。\n  TAWM 对比成为 novelty 支柱：\"dt-conditioning 在 MPC 中成功（TAWM, ICML 2025）但在 imagination 中失败——我们提供首个机制解释。\"\n  跨环境泛化声明全部删除，替换为 extensive limitations section 讨论 Cheetah/Cartpole 为何动力学不同\n  （reward density、state dimensionality、RSSM fidelity characteristics）。\n  仍可投 CoRL 作为 methodology + single-environment depth 论文，但接收概率下降；需 exceptional writing quality 和 TAWM contrast 支撑 novelty。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # WALKER WALK — 已完成实验的 worst-tier 解读\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"复现 CIVO collapse，2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009e_final_eval: 131.08\n      seed1_009e_peak_nve: 4.12\n      seed1_009e_collapse: true\n      seed2_009b_final_eval: 267.93\n      seed2_009b_peak_nve: 2.05\n      seed2_009b_collapse: false\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      nve_gt_1_5x_rate: \"2/2 (100%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据已收集。worst-tier 解读：collapse rate 仅 50%（1/2 独立 seed 崩溃），\n      削弱 \"CIVO 是 deterministic failure\" 的叙事。009b 的自修正（NVE 2.05x@25K → 0.38x@105K）\n      证明 CIVO 反馈环并非不可逆——早期训练随机性决定路径分叉。这迫使论文用语从\n      \"trained dt_emb causes collapse\" 改为 \"trained dt_emb reliably triggers pathological\n      overestimation (NVE>1.5x), with collapse as a stochastic consequence\"。\n      当 Cheetah 无法复现该模式时，50% collapse rate 的统计力量进一步被质疑。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d config cross-seed comparison\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0 (008d)\", \"Seed 1 (009e)\", \"Seed 2 (009b)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Peak NVE (35K+)\", \"2.09x@45K\", \"4.12x@55K\", \"1.62x@45K\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"Yes@55K\", \"Yes@55K\", \"No (self-correct)\"]\n          - [\"Final eval@105K\", \"82.7 (55K stop)\", \"131.1\", \"267.9\"]\n          - [\"NVE trajectory\", \"accelerating\", \"accelerating\", \"transient peak → decline\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE 轨迹对比图：seed 0/1 加速发散 vs seed 2 自修正。标注 1.5x threshold 和 35K cutoff\"\n    analysis: >\n      Walker 内 NVE>1.5x diagnostic 仍有 2/2 sensitivity（trained seeds 全部 exceed），\n      但 collapse 的 stochastic nature 限制了 practical significance。当 Cheetah 数据加入\n      后（0/3 exceed 1.5x），threshold 的跨环境推广将失败。Worst-tier 下这组数据\n      退化为 Walker-specific 机制证据而非 general vulnerability 证据。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"复现因果控制稳定性，2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009f_status: \"killed (incomplete)\"\n      seed2_009c_final_eval: 148.34\n      seed2_009c_peak_nve: 1.26\n      seed2_009c_trend: \"peak 359@75K → decline to 148@105K\"\n      seed2_009c_collapse: false\n      protection_robust: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据：009f 被 kill（无完整数据），009c 在 75K 后持续下降至 148（vs baseline 916，仅 16%）。\n      虽然 009c 的 NVE 始终 <1.5x（peak 1.26x@25K），符合 \"no CIVO\" 判定，但绝对性能极差。\n      Worst-tier 解读：dt_embed_dim=0 的 \"保护\" 极不 robust——seed 0 恢复到 503 而 seed 2 跌至 148。\n      保护机制是 seed-dependent 的，008f 不是可靠方案。因果方向（trained dt_emb → CIVO）仍成立\n      （两个 seed 均 NVE<1.5x），但 practical value 有限。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f config cross-seed\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0 (008f)\", \"Seed 2 (009c)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Peak NVE\", \"1.02x@25K\", \"1.26x@25K\"]\n          - [\"Final eval@105K\", \"503\", \"148\"]\n          - [\"Recovery pattern\", \"Zigzag → 503\", \"Peak 359@75K → decline\"]\n          - [\"vs baseline\", \"-45%\", \"-84%\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      009c 的衰退说明去掉 dt_embedding 虽阻止 CIVO 但不保证学习成功——reward prediction\n      退化（MAE 75x baseline）本身就是严重代价。Worst-tier 下，这组数据用于因果论证\n      但不支持任何 practical recommendation。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"C6 mitigation multi-seed validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 137.0\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_mechanism: \"non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑)\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      c6_status: \"PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据。s1 成功（95% baseline），s2 在 85-105K 崩溃（715→452→137），但机制与\n      经典 CIVO 不同：s2 是 eval-driven（eval 先跌，value 稳定，entropy ↑），而 008d 是\n      value-driven（value 爆炸，eval 后跌，entropy ↓）。009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定\n      （618→596→836），排除 seed 脆弱性。Worst-tier 解读：dt=1 imagination 未降低\n      collapse rate（与 dt=2 同为 50%），C6 mitigation 被 falsify。Trained dt_embedding\n      通过 Pathway B（non-CIVO policy instability）绕过 dt=1 保护。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 Pathway A vs Pathway B\"\n        headers: [\"Feature\", \"008d s0 (Pathway A: CIVO)\", \"008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B: non-CIVO)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Value change\", \"+130% explosion\", \"+13% stable\"]\n          - [\"Eval change\", \"后跌 -43%\", \"先跌 -81%\"]\n          - [\"NVE driver\", \"Value 分子驱动\", \"Eval 分母驱动\"]\n          - [\"Actor entropy\", \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\", \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\"]\n          - [\"Mechanism\", \"Critic overestimate → actor exploit\", \"Eval crash → value lag\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双 pathway 对比图：value/eval/entropy 三轨并列，008d s0 vs 008e_v3 s2\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 partially falsified 是 worst-tier 最关键的负面结果。论文需重新定位 trained dt_embedding\n      为 \"multi-pathway vulnerability creator\"，而非仅 CIVO trigger。但 Pathway B 机制\n      尚不充分理解——如果 plan_016 显示仅 1/4 崩溃，Pathway B 可能退化为 seed variance。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否为 CIVO 必要条件\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_eval_105K: 204.2\n      nve_range: \"0.39-0.47\"\n      collapse: false\n      collapse_mechanism: \"gradient starvation (actor_loss→0)\"\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据（exp_015b）。Frozen dt_emb 导致 gradient starvation：随机初始化的 dt_embedding\n      不训练，为 RSSM 提供无信息 conditioning→critic 系统性低估（NVE 0.39-0.47x），\n      actor loss 趋近零，学习停滞。eval 在 80-238 间剧烈波动，无稳定收敛。\n      Worst-tier 解读：确认了一个消融点（frozen ≠ trained ≠ absent），但引入新失败模式\n      （gradient starvation），不能作为 mitigation。论文仅能作为 mechanism isolation 证据：\n      dt_emb 的 training 过程本身驱动 CIVO。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Frozen dt_emb 的 gradient starvation 是 worst-tier 下的一个 \"ugly control\"——\n      它证明了 dt_emb training 是 CIVO 必要条件，但方式不够 clean（引入新问题而非\n      neutral baseline）。论文中需小心呈现：这是析因矩阵中的一个消融点，而非独立 finding。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # WALKER WALK — 真正未完成的实验\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"复现 value growth suppression，2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 460\n        45K: 510\n        55K: 440\n        65K: 550\n        75K: 480\n        85K: 530\n        95K: 520\n        105K: 700\n      seed1_nve_range_55K_105K: [0.60, 0.85]\n      seed1_final_eval: 700\n      seed1_vs_baseline_105K: \"-23.5%\"\n      seed2_eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 420\n        45K: 480\n        55K: 400\n        65K: 470\n        75K: 430\n        85K: 510\n        95K: 490\n        105K: 620\n      seed2_nve_range_55K_105K: [0.55, 0.80]\n      seed2_final_eval: 620\n      seed2_vs_baseline_105K: \"-32.3%\"\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 699\n      cross_seed_nve_mean_105K: 0.63\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 下 C3 在 Walker 内仍 hold，但 variance 更大。Seed 0 (778@105K, 85% baseline)\n      是最优 seed；seed 1-2 预计较低（700/620@105K，76%/68% baseline），因为 subsample OFF +\n      untrained dt_emb 的保护性依赖 RSSM 在 dt=1 数据上的收敛质量——不同 seed 的 RSSM\n      初始化影响 dt=1 prediction 精度，进而影响 value calibration。Normalized v/e 仍一致\n      低于 1.0x（无 CIVO），但绝对性能比 seed 0 差，拉低 cross-seed IQM。\n      在 worst-tier 下这不影响 C3 的定性结论，但 Agarwal et al. (2021) IQM + CI 会更宽。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Eval@105K\", \"778\", \"700\", \"620\", \"699\"]\n          - [\"vs baseline\", \"-15%\", \"-24%\", \"-32%\", \"-24%\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.59x\", \"0.65x\", \"0.72x\", \"0.65x\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"No\", \"No\", \"No\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed 学习曲线叠加，均显示 zigzag 但幅度和收敛点不同\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 在 Walker 内 robust（3/3 seeds NVE<1.0x，无崩溃），但跨 seed 绝对性能变化大\n      （620-778，22% 跨距）。Worst-tier 下，这组数据仅 reinforces Walker-specific 结论。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"缩窄 Pathway B collapse probability estimate\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 830\n      seed3_nve_105K: 0.78\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed4_eval_105K: 790\n      seed4_nve_105K: 0.82\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      total_collapse_rate: \"1/4 (25%)\"\n      pathway_b_interpretation: \"closer to seed variance than systematic pathway\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 核心假设之一：\"Pathway B control experiment reveals 008e_v3_s2 collapse\n      was closer to random seed variance than a systematic second pathway\"。Seed 3-4\n      均不崩溃，collapse rate 从 1/2 降至 1/4（25%）。在 4 个 seed 中仅 1 个崩溃，\n      且该崩溃的机制签名（entropy ↑, eval-driven）与 CIVO 不同，更接近 policy\n      optimization 的随机脆弱性。这削弱 \"multiple vulnerability pathways\" 叙事——\n      Pathway B 不是 systematic mechanism 而是 seed-specific instability。\n      论文需要 honest reporting：trained dt_emb + dt=1 imag 的 collapse rate ~25%，\n      无法确定是否显著高于 baseline（baseline 0/2 seeds 崩溃，但 n 太小无法做统计检验）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 all seeds\"\n        headers: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE@105K\", \"Collapse?\", \"Mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed 1 (s1)\", \"869.9\", \"0.80x\", \"No\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"Seed 2 (s2)\", \"137.0\", \"3.78x\", \"Yes\", \"Eval-driven (Pathway B)\"]\n          - [\"Seed 3 (pred)\", \"830\", \"0.78x\", \"No\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"Seed 4 (pred)\", \"790\", \"0.82x\", \"No\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed 学习曲线 + NVE 轨迹，标注 seed 2 崩溃点及与其余 3 seeds 的分歧\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/4 collapse rate 在 worst-tier 下严重削弱 Pathway B 论述。论文可能需要从\n      \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\" 退回到\n      \"trained dt_embedding reliably triggers CIVO (Pathway A, blocked by dt=1 imag);\n      rare policy instability events (1/4 seeds) may or may not be related\"。\n      这实际上部分 salvages dt=1 mitigation（3/4 seeds 成功，接近 baseline），\n      但 honest reporting 要求承认 n=4 统计力量不足。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"不同 NVE 阈值的分类精度，0 GPU 成本\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_only:\n        threshold_1_3x:\n          accuracy: 0.80\n          sensitivity: 1.0\n          specificity: 0.50\n          note: \"1 FP (009c@25K NVE=1.26 borderline, 但 35K+ 限定后为 TN)\"\n        threshold_1_5x:\n          accuracy: 1.0\n          sensitivity: 1.0\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"4/4 perfect at 35K+\"\n        threshold_1_7x:\n          accuracy: 0.80\n          sensitivity: 0.67\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"009b peak NVE=1.62x barely above 1.7x? Actually no, 1.62<1.7 → FN\"\n        threshold_2_0x:\n          accuracy: 0.80\n          sensitivity: 0.67\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"009b peak 2.05x@25K excluded by 35K+ rule; 1.62x@45K<2.0 → FN\"\n        auroc: 0.98\n      cross_env_walker_cheetah:\n        threshold_1_5x:\n          accuracy: 0.64\n          sensitivity: 0.40\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"Walker 2/2 trained→TP; Cheetah 0/3 trained→FN; all untrained→TN\"\n        auroc: 0.72\n      cross_env_all_three:\n        threshold_1_5x:\n          accuracy: 0.58\n          sensitivity: 0.29\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"仅 Walker 2/7 trained seeds 被检出\"\n        auroc: 0.65\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 内 1.5x threshold 完美分离（AUROC~0.98），这是 existing data 的强结论。\n      但在 worst-tier 下，Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb seeds NVE 全部 <1.5x（范围 0.8-1.4x），\n      因为 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity characteristics 不同——reward density 更高、state\n      dynamics 更 smooth，dt_emb 的 observation decoder 梯度不产生同样的 systematic bias。\n      这导致 threshold 在 Cheetah 上产生大量 false negatives（degradation 发生但 NVE\n      不超标）。Cross-env AUROC 从 0.98 降至 ~0.72，远低于 diagnostic tool 的实用标准。\n      论文必须 honest report：\"NVE>1.5x is a reliable Walker Walk diagnostic but does NOT\n      generalize to Cheetah Run, where degradation manifests through different dynamics.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NVE 1.5x threshold cross-environment performance\"\n        headers: [\"Environment\", \"Trained Seeds\", \"TP\", \"FN\", \"Untrained Seeds\", \"TN\", \"FP\", \"Accuracy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3\", \"3\", \"0\", \"2\", \"2\", \"0\", \"5/5=1.00\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3\", \"3\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3/6=0.50\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3\", \"3\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3/6=0.50\"]\n          - [\"Cross-env total\", \"9\", \"3\", \"6\", \"8\", \"8\", \"0\", \"11/17=0.65\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC 曲线：Walker-only (AUROC=0.98) vs cross-env (AUROC=0.72)\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE 方法论是 worst-tier 下论文的 second contribution pillar，但必须诚实定位为\n      \"validated in Walker Walk, proposed for broader adoption with caveats\"。跨环境失败\n      不否定方法论本身——而是揭示 CIVO 机制的 environment-specificity。论文应讨论\n      为何 Cheetah 的 NVE pattern 不同（reward density、RSSM fidelity characteristics），\n      将 negative result 转化为 diagnostic insight。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CHEETAH RUN — 跨环境泛化（worst-tier 核心失败区域）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"第二 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_final_eval: 849.8\n      seed1_status: \"DONE (exp_010a)\"\n      seed2_final_eval: 825\n      seed3_final_eval: 862\n      cross_seed_mean: 846\n      cross_seed_std: 19\n      ve_ratio_stable: \"0.65-0.72 from 135K+\"\n      ve_ratio_trajectory:\n        25K: 0.09\n        35K: 0.19\n        45K: 0.28\n        55K: 0.36\n        65K: 0.47\n        75K: 0.57\n        85K: 0.63\n        95K: 0.66\n        105K: 0.68\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 在 DreamerV3 上训练正常，peak ~850。Seed 1 已完成（849.8）。\n      Cheetah 的 reward 是 forward velocity（dense, smooth），收敛特性与 Walker Walk 类似\n      但 v/e trajectory 略低（Cheetah 的 discount structure 和 reward scale 不同）。\n      Baseline 本身不受 worst-tier 影响——环境正常运行是所有后续实验的前提。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 确立 Cheetah Run 的参考线。v/e calibration（~0.68@105K）与 Walker（~0.656@105K）\n      高度一致，为 NVE 比较提供合理基础。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"复现 CIVO collapse in Cheetah — worst-tier 预测失败\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 190\n          25K: 370\n          35K: 520\n          45K: 490\n          55K: 440\n          65K: 400\n          75K: 380\n          85K: 360\n          95K: 370\n          105K: 385\n        value_trajectory:\n          25K: 28\n          35K: 85\n          45K: 120\n          55K: 140\n          65K: 145\n          75K: 140\n          85K: 130\n          95K: 125\n          105K: 128\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.94\n          45K: 0.92\n          55K: 0.95\n          65K: 0.83\n          75K: 0.72\n          85K: 0.68\n          95K: 0.65\n          105K: 0.63\n        collapse: false\n        peak_nve: 0.95\n        pattern: \"gradual decline without value acceleration\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 480\n          45K: 430\n          55K: 380\n          65K: 350\n          75K: 340\n          85K: 360\n          95K: 375\n          105K: 390\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 1.25\n          45K: 1.30\n          55K: 1.28\n          65K: 1.15\n          75K: 0.98\n          85K: 0.92\n          95K: 0.88\n          105K: 0.85\n        collapse: false\n        peak_nve: 1.30\n        pattern: \"mild overestimation plateau then decline — not accelerating\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 550\n          45K: 520\n          55K: 470\n          65K: 430\n          75K: 410\n          85K: 420\n          95K: 430\n          105K: 445\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.82\n          45K: 0.85\n          55K: 0.90\n          65K: 0.87\n          75K: 0.80\n          85K: 0.78\n          95K: 0.75\n          105K: 0.74\n        collapse: false\n        peak_nve: 0.90\n        pattern: \"value suppression — similar to Walker dt=4\"\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_nve_max: 1.30\n      cross_seed_nve_mean_at_55K: 1.04\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 407\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-52%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 核心假设：\"Cheetah Run shows performance degradation with dt>1 but NVE pattern\n      differs\"。三个 seed 均显示 degradation（eval 407 平均 vs baseline 846，-52%），但\n      NVE 模式与 Walker 定性不同：\n      (1) Seed 0 (NVE 0.63-0.95x)：value suppression 模式，类似 Walker dt=4——RSSM 在\n          Cheetah 的 dt>1 prediction 质量差导致 critic underestimate 而非 overestimate。\n          Cheetah 的 velocity-based reward 结构使 dt>1 reward prediction 偏差方向不同。\n      (2) Seed 1 (NVE peak 1.30x)：温和过估计但不加速。NVE 在 35-55K 达到 1.25-1.30x\n          后自行下降至 0.85x。与 Walker 008d 的加速发散（1.71x→2.09x→4.12x）形成鲜明对比。\n          Cheetah 的 RSSM 可能在 dt>1 有更好的 self-correction 能力（state space 更规则）。\n      (3) Seed 2 (NVE 0.74-0.90x)：纯 value suppression。\n      没有任何 seed 的 NVE 超过 1.5x → 1.5x threshold 在 Cheetah 上完全失效（0/3 detected）。\n      Degradation 确实存在但不是 CIVO——更可能是 learning signal reduction (C5) + RSSM\n      fidelity gap 的混合效应，不伴随 positive feedback loop。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed NVE\"\n        headers: [\"Step\", \"Seed 0 NVE\", \"Seed 1 NVE\", \"Seed 2 NVE\", \"Walker 008d NVE (ref)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.94\", \"1.25\", \"0.82\", \"1.71\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"0.92\", \"1.30\", \"0.85\", \"2.09\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"0.95\", \"1.28\", \"0.90\", \"4.12\"]\n          - [\"65K\", \"0.83\", \"1.15\", \"0.87\", \"(collapsed)\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"0.63\", \"0.85\", \"0.74\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah vs Walker NVE 轨迹对比：Walker 加速发散 vs Cheetah 平稳/下降\"\n      - \"Cheetah 3-seed eval 曲线 + baseline reference\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst-tier 的 defining result。Degradation 存在但 CIVO 缺失。论文必须承认：\n      \"The CIVO mechanism (accelerating NVE feedback loop) is environment-specific. In Cheetah\n      Run, trained dt_embedding degrades performance through a different mechanism — likely\n      learning signal quality degradation without the positive feedback loop observed in Walker.\"\n      Limitations section 需讨论 Cheetah 为何不同：(a) reward 结构（pure velocity vs\n      complex locomotion reward），(b) state space dimensionality 和 smoothness，\n      (c) RSSM 对不同 dynamics 的 fidelity characteristics。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Cheetah 因果控制——worst-tier 预测无 clean separation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 470\n          55K: 400\n          75K: 370\n          105K: 410\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.75\n          55K: 0.90\n          75K: 0.85\n          105K: 0.70\n        pattern: \"similar degradation to trained dt_emb\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 510\n          55K: 430\n          75K: 400\n          105K: 440\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.68\n          55K: 0.80\n          75K: 0.75\n          105K: 0.65\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 490\n          55K: 420\n          75K: 380\n          105K: 380\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 1.10\n          55K: 1.05\n          75K: 0.90\n          105K: 0.82\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 410\n      cross_seed_nve_range: [0.65, 1.10]\n      nve_overlap_with_trained: \"substantial (trained range [0.63, 1.30] vs untrained [0.65, 1.10])\"\n      vs_trained_dt_emb_eval_diff: \"+0.7% (not significant)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 假设：\"NVE 1.5x threshold doesn't separate trained/untrained in Cheetah\"。\n      去掉 dt_embedding 后 Cheetah 的 eval 和 NVE 与 trained dt_emb 配置几乎无差异\n      （eval 410 vs 407, NVE 0.65-1.10 vs 0.63-1.30）。原因：Cheetah 的 degradation\n      根源是 learning signal reduction（subsample ON 导致有效 transition 数减半）而非\n      dt_embedding-driven CIVO。在 Walker 中，去掉 dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO feedback loop，\n      产生 dramatic 差异（008f NVE<1.0 vs 008d NVE>2.0）；在 Cheetah 中，没有\n      CIVO feedback loop 需要阻止，所以去掉 dt_emb 不产生 significant effect。\n      这是 worst-tier 下最难处理的结果——直接否定 C2 因果链在 Cheetah 上的适用性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah: trained vs no dt_emb\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Trained dt_emb (plan_021)\", \"No dt_emb (plan_022)\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Eval mean@105K\", \"407\", \"410\", \"+0.7% (ns)\"]\n          - [\"NVE range (35K+)\", \"[0.63, 1.30]\", \"[0.65, 1.10]\", \"overlapping\"]\n          - [\"Collapse rate\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"identical\"]\n          - [\"NVE>1.5x rate\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"identical\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained vs untrained dt_emb: eval + NVE 并排对比，标注 overlap region\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 \"no separation\" 是 worst-tier 最 damaging 的 cross-env negative result。\n      论文需要解释为什么 Walker 的因果机制不 transfer：dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 的\n      observation decoder 梯度路径可能不产生同向 systematic bias，因为 Cheetah 的\n      state space structure（关节速度为主导 observable）让 RSSM 对 dt>1 的 prediction\n      error 分布更 uniform（不集中在特定 decoder head），无法形成 amplification loop。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Cheetah value growth suppression — worst-tier 预测无 clear advantage\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 490\n          55K: 430\n          75K: 450\n          105K: 520\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.80\n          55K: 0.75\n          75K: 0.70\n          105K: 0.65\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 520\n          55K: 460\n          75K: 480\n          105K: 550\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.72\n          55K: 0.78\n          75K: 0.68\n          105K: 0.60\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 480\n          55K: 440\n          75K: 430\n          105K: 490\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.85\n          55K: 0.82\n          75K: 0.75\n          105K: 0.70\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 520\n      vs_baseline: \"-39%\"\n      vs_trained_dt_emb: \"+28% (520 vs 407)\"\n      vs_no_dt_emb: \"+27% (520 vs 410)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Subsample OFF 保留完整 learning signal，所以 eval 高于 plan_021/022（520 vs 407/410）。\n      但这个提升来自 learning signal preservation（C5），不是 value suppression（C3）。\n      NVE 在 0.60-0.85x 范围，与 plan_022 (0.65-1.10) 有 overlap。Worst-tier 解读：\n      C3 在 Cheetah 上不能 cleanly 验证，因为 baseline comparison 被 subsample 差异混淆。\n      To isolate C3 需要 subsample ON + untrained dt_emb（但 Walker 已有 008c/008e_v3\n      数据做此对比）。在 Cheetah 上，所有 dt>1 配置都 degrades，无论 dt_emb 状态如何。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah untrained dt_emb 的 eval 提升主要归因于 subsample OFF（保留学习信号），\n      非 value suppression 机制。C3 声明在 Cheetah 上 confounded。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CARTPOLE SWINGUP — 第三环境（worst-tier 同样失败）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"非 locomotion 环境 baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_final_eval: 840\n      seed1_final_eval: 820\n      seed2_final_eval: 855\n      cross_seed_mean: 838\n      ve_ratio_stable: \"0.60-0.68 from 135K+\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DreamerV3 上的 well-solved benchmark，baseline ~840。\n      V/e ratio 收敛到 ~0.64，略低于 Walker/Cheetah，因为 Cartpole 的 sparse initial\n      reward（swingup 前 reward 极低）使 value function 在 early training 更保守。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常。Cartpole 的 non-locomotion dynamics（pendulum + cart）\n      为跨环境泛化测试提供了不同 task family。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"复现 CIVO collapse in Cartpole — worst-tier 预测 no CIVO\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_105K: 320\n        peak_nve: 0.75\n        pattern: \"value suppression — critic under-estimates\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_105K: 280\n        peak_nve: 0.90\n        pattern: \"learning failure — low asymptote\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_105K: 350\n        peak_nve: 0.65\n        pattern: \"value suppression\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 317\n      vs_baseline: \"-62%\"\n      collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n      nve_max: 0.90\n      nve_gt_1_5x: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 的 sparse reward structure 使 dt>1 transitions 的 reward prediction\n      几乎无信息（swingup 前大量 near-zero reward）。Trained dt_emb 不会产生 CIVO 因为：\n      (1) RSSM 对 dt>1 的 reward prediction 偏差方向是 under-estimation（sparse reward\n          的高 reward events 在 dt>1 步后更难预测，导致 systematic negative bias）；\n      (2) Observation decoder 梯度集中在 pendulum angle 上（单一关键 observable），\n          不像 Walker 的 multi-head gradient（orientations/velocity/height）能形成\n          amplification；\n      (3) Cartpole 的 state space（4D: cart pos/vel + pole angle/vel）远小于\n          Walker（24D+），RSSM 的 dt>1 fidelity gap 更小。\n      结果是 degradation 但以 value suppression/learning failure 形式出现，无 CIVO signature。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole trained dt_emb NVE\"\n        headers: [\"Seed\", \"Peak NVE\", \"NVE@105K\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0\", \"0.75\", \"0.60\", \"No\", \"Value suppression\"]\n          - [\"1\", \"0.90\", \"0.70\", \"No\", \"Learning failure\"]\n          - [\"2\", \"0.65\", \"0.55\", \"No\", \"Value suppression\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的 NVE pattern（全部 <1.0x）与 Walker 的 CIVO（>1.5x accelerating）和\n      Cheetah 的 mixed pattern（0.6-1.3x stable）都不同。三个环境三种 failure mode：\n      Walker=CIVO, Cheetah=mild overestimation/plateau, Cartpole=value suppression。\n      这证明 dt>1 degradation 是 universal 但 mechanism 是 environment-specific。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Cartpole 因果控制\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 310\n      seed1_eval_105K: 290\n      seed2_eval_105K: 340\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 313\n      vs_trained_dt_emb: \"-1.3% (not significant)\"\n      nve_range: [0.55, 0.85]\n      nve_overlap_with_trained: \"complete overlap\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 类似，去掉 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 上不产生 significant 差异。\n      Degradation 根源是 learning signal reduction（C5），dt_emb 不是 primary factor。\n      Eval 313 vs trained 317，差异在噪声范围内。NVE 完全 overlap。\n      Walker 中 008f vs 008d 的 dramatic 差异（NVE 0.97x vs 2.09x）在 Cartpole\n      不可复现——因为 Cartpole 没有 CIVO feedback loop 需要 dt_emb 来 trigger。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的 \"no separation\" 进一步确认：CIVO 是 Walker-specific phenomenon。\n      Cross-env data 现在显示 3 environments 中仅 1 个有 CIVO。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 分析类实验（0 GPU 或低 GPU）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment-specific characteristics\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 10.2\n        dt2_obs_mse: 18.5\n        obs_gap: 1.81\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.008\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.012\n        reward_gap: 1.50\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 15.8\n        dt2_obs_mse: 22.3\n        obs_gap: 1.41\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.035\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.065\n        reward_gap: 1.86\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 9.5\n        dt2_obs_mse: 19.8\n        obs_gap: 2.08\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.52\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.54\n        reward_gap: 1.04\n      walker_vs_cheetah_obs_gap_comparison:\n        walker_baseline: 2.04\n        cheetah_baseline: 1.81\n        walker_trained: 1.30\n        cheetah_trained: 1.41\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 与 Walker 数值接近但分布不同。关键差异：\n      (1) Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb reward gap (1.86x) 低于 Walker (2.78x)——\n          Cheetah 的 velocity reward 更 smooth，dt_emb 不会像 Walker 那样在 reward head\n          产生 large systematic bias。但注意 Walker 的 reward gradient = 0（by architecture），\n          所以 reward gap 不是 CIVO 的直接驱动因素。\n      (2) Cheetah 的 obs_gap (1.81x baseline, 1.41x trained) 与 Walker (2.04x, 1.30x) \n          类似，但 obs MSE 的绝对值更低——Cheetah 的 state space 更规则，RSSM 建模质量更好。\n      (3) Cheetah trained dt_emb 的 dt1 abs obs_MSE (15.8) 显著低于 Walker (41.31)——\n          模型没有像 Walker 那样因为 CIVO 而全面崩塌。\n      Worst-tier 解读：fidelity gap 存在但不 sufficient to trigger CIVO in Cheetah。\n      机制的 environment-specificity 体现在 fidelity gap 如何通过 gradient pathways\n      传播到 value function——Walker 的 multi-head gradient structure 放大 bias，\n      Cheetah 的更 uniform gradient 不放大。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment RSSM fidelity comparison\"\n        headers: [\"Model\", \"Env\", \"dt1 obs_MSE\", \"dt2 obs_MSE\", \"obs gap\", \"reward gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"Walker\", \"13.49\", \"27.50\", \"2.04x\", \"1.56x\"]\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"Cheetah\", \"10.2\", \"18.5\", \"1.81x\", \"1.50x\"]\n          - [\"Trained dt_emb\", \"Walker\", \"41.31\", \"53.67\", \"1.30x\", \"2.78x\"]\n          - [\"Trained dt_emb\", \"Cheetah\", \"15.8\", \"22.3\", \"1.41x\", \"1.86x\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb\", \"Walker\", \"8.01\", \"22.04\", \"2.75x\", \"1.01x\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb\", \"Cheetah\", \"9.5\", \"19.8\", \"2.08x\", \"1.04x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-env RSSM fidelity heatmap: obs_MSE × reward_MAE 四象限，标注 CIVO/non-CIVO regions\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity gap 是 necessary but not sufficient for CIVO。Cheetah 有 gap 但\n      无 CIVO 放大。论文需讨论 gradient pathway structure 作为 missing mediator。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Walker + Cheetah actor entropy trajectory 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_civo_collapsed_008d:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"8.2→-1.9→-3.5→-4.6→-4.9\"\n        pattern: \"entropy ↓: policy becomes deterministic during CIVO\"\n      walker_pathway_b_008e_v3_s2:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-5.1→-5.2→-5.2→-4.5→-3.8\"\n        pattern: \"entropy ↑: policy destabilizes (opposite of CIVO)\"\n      walker_healthy_008a:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-4.2→-4.5→-4.6→-4.7→-4.8\"\n        pattern: \"entropy stable: normal policy convergence\"\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-3.8→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2→-4.3\"\n        pattern: \"entropy stable: no CIVO or Pathway B signature\"\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-3.7→-3.9→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2\"\n        pattern: \"entropy stable: indistinguishable from trained\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 在 Walker 中是 CIVO 和 Pathway B 的 discriminating signature：\n      CIVO → entropy ↓（critic overestimate 让 actor converge to exploitative policy），\n      Pathway B → entropy ↑（policy destabilization，actor 失去 coherent strategy）。\n      在 Cheetah 中，因为没有 CIVO 或 Pathway B，所有配置的 entropy trajectory \n      几乎一致（stable decline），无法作为 diagnostic tool。这进一步确认 Cheetah 的\n      degradation 机制不同——没有 actor 层面的 pathological dynamics。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Walker entropy 三轨对比（CIVO↓ / Pathway B↑ / healthy→）vs Cheetah 无差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy analysis 在 Walker 内是有力 diagnostic，但在 Cheetah 上无差异性。\n      论文可呈现为 Walker-specific finding。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"V(s) vs MC return 分布分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_divergence:\n        value_mean: 97.5\n        mc_return_mean: 35\n        ks_statistic: 0.72\n        pattern: \"right-shifted value distribution — systematic overestimation\"\n      walker_008a_calibration:\n        value_mean: 280\n        mc_return_mean: 550\n        ks_statistic: 0.35\n        pattern: \"left-shifted but not pathological — conservative value\"\n      cheetah_trained_divergence:\n        value_mean: 140\n        mc_return_mean: 180\n        ks_statistic: 0.28\n        pattern: \"mild underestimation — no systematic overestimation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 008d 的 V(s) 分布系统性右偏（overestimate），与 MC return 严重脱节\n      （KS=0.72）。这是 CIVO 的 direct evidence。Cheetah trained dt_emb 的 V(s)\n      分布仅轻微左偏（underestimate, KS=0.28），不存在 systematic overestimation。\n      Worst-tier 下，分布分析强化了 \"CIVO is Walker-specific\" 的结论。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"V(s) vs MC return 散点图 + violin plot: Walker 008d (divergent) vs Cheetah (aligned)\"\n    analysis: >\n      分布分析是比 v/e ratio 更 informative 的 proxy，但在 worst-tier 下仅确认\n      已知结论。投入 1 GPU-hour 的 ROI 有限。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"learned dt_emb vectors 的 dt=1 vs dt=2 similarity evolution\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_initial_cosine: 0.85\n      walker_trained_30K_cosine: 0.42\n      walker_trained_60K_cosine: 0.28\n      walker_trend: \"diverging — dt=1 and dt=2 embeddings become increasingly dissimilar\"\n      cheetah_initial_cosine: 0.85\n      cheetah_trained_30K_cosine: 0.55\n      cheetah_trained_60K_cosine: 0.48\n      cheetah_trend: \"partial divergence — less separation than Walker\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 中 dt_emb 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 vectors 快速分化（cosine 0.85→0.28），\n      说明 network 积极利用 dt conditioning 来做 specialized predictions——这是\n      CIVO 的前提条件。Cheetah 中分化较缓（0.85→0.48），说明 dt_emb 被利用程度\n      较低——network 未充分 specialize on dt information，因此不会形成 strong\n      dt-dependent value bias。这与 Cheetah 的 observation decoder 梯度更 uniform\n      的假设一致——没有足够的 gradient signal 来 push dt_emb 向 high-separation direction。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"dt_emb cosine similarity vs training step: Walker (fast divergence) vs Cheetah (slow)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine analysis 提供了为什么 CIVO 在 Cheetah 不发生的 additional mechanistic insight：\n      dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中学到的 dt 区分度更低，减少了 condition-dependent bias 的\n      severity。可作为 Discussion section 的 supporting analysis。0 GPU cost，值得做。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # EXPLORATORY / MITIGATION\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"RSSM 不确定性门控 imagination 截断——Walker Walk pilot\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 540\n      vs_baseline: \"-41%\"\n      nve_peak: 1.15\n      collapse: false\n      truncation_rate_at_dt2: 0.35\n      effective_horizon_mean: 11.2\n      issues:\n        - \"RSSM ensemble disagreement 校准不准——在 dt=1 transitions 上也频繁触发截断\"\n        - \"有效 horizon 从 15 降至 ~11，减少了 long-range credit assignment\"\n        - \"稳定但性能远低于 008e_v3 seed 1 (870) 和 baseline (916)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RSSM 本身不提供 well-calibrated uncertainty estimates（DreamerV3 使用 single RSSM，\n      不是 ensemble）。Pilot 需要额外实现 RSSM ensemble 或使用 KL divergence as proxy。\n      在 worst-tier 下，uncertainty estimate 噪声大：dt=1 transitions 的不确定性\n      也偶尔偏高（false truncation），而 dt>1 transitions 的不确定性不总是偏高\n      （missed truncation）。Net effect: truncation 防止了最严重的 collapse（NVE 不超 1.5x），\n      但 over-truncation 缩短有效 horizon，损失 long-range learning signal。\n      Eval 540 好于 008d collapse (83) 但远低于 008e_v3 success (870)。\n      不适合作为 paper contribution——implementation complexity 高但 benefit 有限。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Uncertainty truncation 是 \"reasonable but noisy\" 的 mitigation。在 worst-tier 下\n      不足以写入论文——更适合 future work section 的 one-sentence mention。\n      CoRL deadline 前不值得投入更多 GPU。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"第三 DMC locomotion 环境——worst-tier 预测：P2 优先级，可能不跑\"\n    expected_results:\n      likely_status: \"NOT RUN before CoRL deadline (P2 priority)\"\n      if_run:\n        baseline_mean: 250\n        trained_dt_emb_mean: 120\n        trained_dt_emb_nve_pattern: \"mixed — some seeds >1.0x, none >1.5x\"\n        no_dt_emb_mean: 130\n        separation: \"minimal\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 sparse reward + contact-rich dynamics，DreamerV3 baseline 仅 ~250\n      （远低于 Walker/Cheetah）。在 worst-tier 下，即使跑了，低 baseline 性能使得\n      v/e ratio 极不稳定（分母小），NVE 信噪比差，无法得出 clean 结论。\n      此外，45 GPU-hours 的预算在 13 天 deadline 前不值得投入——这些资源应用于\n      确保 Walker 数据的 presentation quality。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      P2 实验在 worst-tier 下应果断放弃。论文不需要第三个 negative result\n      来说明 CIVO 是 environment-specific。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CROSS-CUTTING ANALYSIS\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Full cross-environment summary table\"\n    plan_id: \"N/A (synthesis)\"\n    description: \"综合所有环境的 CIVO 检测结果\"\n    expected_results:\n      environments_with_confirmed_civo: 1\n      walker_walk:\n        civo_confirmed: true\n        nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2 to 2/3 seeds\"\n        full_sgs_nve: 1.00\n        mechanism: \"observation-decoder-driven gradient amplification\"\n      cheetah_run:\n        civo_confirmed: false\n        nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: \"0/3 (0%)\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        degradation: \"yes (-52% baseline)\"\n        mechanism: \"learning signal reduction + mild fidelity gap, no positive feedback loop\"\n      cartpole_swingup:\n        civo_confirmed: false\n        nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: \"0/3 (0%)\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        degradation: \"yes (-62% baseline)\"\n        mechanism: \"value suppression from sparse reward + dt>1 prediction noise\"\n      cross_env_threshold_accuracy: 0.65\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 的 defining outcome：只有 Walker Walk 确认 CIVO。Cheetah 和 Cartpole\n      都显示 dt>1 degradation 但通过不同机制。1.5x NVE threshold 在 Walker 内完美\n      但跨环境仅 0.65 accuracy。这迫使论文完全退守 single-environment depth story。\n      贡献变为：(1) Walker Walk 的 rigorous factorial diagnosis，(2) NVE methodology\n      （validated in Walker, proposed with caveats），(3) gradient-level evidence\n      （Full-SGS），(4) TAWM contrast（MPC vs imagination）。\n      Drop 所有 \"general architectural vulnerability\" 语言。\n      Add extensive limitations section 讨论 environment-specificity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment CIVO summary\"\n        headers: [\"Environment\", \"Degradation?\", \"CIVO (NVE>1.5x)?\", \"Collapse?\", \"Mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"Yes (-5% to -85%)\", \"Yes (3/3 seeds)\", \"Yes (1-2/3)\", \"CIVO + Pathway B\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"Yes (-52%)\", \"No (0/3 seeds)\", \"No (0/3)\", \"Learning signal + fidelity gap\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"Yes (-62%)\", \"No (0/3 seeds)\", \"No (0/3)\", \"Value suppression\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-env NVE distribution violin plot: Walker (wide, right-skewed >1.5x) vs Cheetah/Cartpole (narrow, centered <1.0x)\"\n    analysis: >\n      论文 framing 最终版：\n      \"We provide the first rigorous factorial diagnosis of why temporal abstraction fails\n      in DreamerV3's imagination-based training, demonstrated in Walker Walk with controlled\n      design. The CIVO mechanism — trained dt-embedding amplifying RSSM fidelity gaps into\n      value overestimation through observation decoder gradients — is confirmed by gradient-level\n      intervention (Full-SGS). Our NVE diagnostic methodology achieves perfect separation\n      in Walker Walk but does not generalize to Cheetah Run or Cartpole Swingup, where\n      degradation proceeds through different mechanisms. This environment-specificity itself\n      is an important finding: temporal abstraction fails universally in our experiments,\n      but the failure mode is environment-dependent, complicating one-size-fits-all solutions.\n      The contrast with TAWM (Nhu et al., ICML 2025), where dt-conditioning succeeds in MPC\n      but fails in imagination, remains the paper's strongest novelty claim regardless of\n      cross-environment generalization.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41539,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41539},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feed3564-d2fd-471f-ba3e-2644a7a39578","uuid":"e477a251-3a17-4aee-8ad4-d5f868ce5f9e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":592670,"duration_api_ms":594413,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Cheetah 未能干净复现 CIVO 模式（NVE 停留在 0.8-1.4x，无加速性过估计签名），Cartpole/ManiSkill3 亦无清晰 CIVO 信号。\n  论文退守为 Walker Walk 单环境深度机制研究。核心贡献重新定位为：\n  (1) 首个严格析因诊断——在 DreamerV3 imagination-based actor-critic 中揭示 temporal abstraction 失败的 specific causal chain；\n  (2) NVE 诊断方法论（Walker 内 4/4 完美分类，提议更广泛使用但承认跨环境泛化受限）；\n  (3) gradient-level 因果证据（Full-SGS NVE 1.00x）证明失败是 observation-decoder-driven 而非 reward-driven——即便限于单环境亦非显然。\n  TAWM 对比成为 novelty 支柱：\"dt-conditioning 在 MPC 中成功（TAWM, ICML 2025）但在 imagination 中失败——我们提供首个机制解释。\"\n  跨环境泛化声明全部删除，替换为 extensive limitations section 讨论 Cheetah/Cartpole 为何动力学不同\n  （reward density、state dimensionality、RSSM fidelity characteristics）。\n  仍可投 CoRL 作为 methodology + single-environment depth 论文，但接收概率下降；需 exceptional writing quality 和 TAWM contrast 支撑 novelty。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # WALKER WALK — 已完成实验的 worst-tier 解读\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"复现 CIVO collapse，2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009e_final_eval: 131.08\n      seed1_009e_peak_nve: 4.12\n      seed1_009e_collapse: true\n      seed2_009b_final_eval: 267.93\n      seed2_009b_peak_nve: 2.05\n      seed2_009b_collapse: false\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      nve_gt_1_5x_rate: \"2/2 (100%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据已收集。worst-tier 解读：collapse rate 仅 50%（1/2 独立 seed 崩溃），\n      削弱 \"CIVO 是 deterministic failure\" 的叙事。009b 的自修正（NVE 2.05x@25K → 0.38x@105K）\n      证明 CIVO 反馈环并非不可逆——早期训练随机性决定路径分叉。这迫使论文用语从\n      \"trained dt_emb causes collapse\" 改为 \"trained dt_emb reliably triggers pathological\n      overestimation (NVE>1.5x), with collapse as a stochastic consequence\"。\n      当 Cheetah 无法复现该模式时，50% collapse rate 的统计力量进一步被质疑。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d config cross-seed comparison\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0 (008d)\", \"Seed 1 (009e)\", \"Seed 2 (009b)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Peak NVE (35K+)\", \"2.09x@45K\", \"4.12x@55K\", \"1.62x@45K\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"Yes@55K\", \"Yes@55K\", \"No (self-correct)\"]\n          - [\"Final eval@105K\", \"82.7 (55K stop)\", \"131.1\", \"267.9\"]\n          - [\"NVE trajectory\", \"accelerating\", \"accelerating\", \"transient peak → decline\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE 轨迹对比图：seed 0/1 加速发散 vs seed 2 自修正。标注 1.5x threshold 和 35K cutoff\"\n    analysis: >\n      Walker 内 NVE>1.5x diagnostic 仍有 2/2 sensitivity（trained seeds 全部 exceed），\n      但 collapse 的 stochastic nature 限制了 practical significance。当 Cheetah 数据加入\n      后（0/3 exceed 1.5x），threshold 的跨环境推广将失败。Worst-tier 下这组数据\n      退化为 Walker-specific 机制证据而非 general vulnerability 证据。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"复现因果控制稳定性，2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009f_status: \"killed (incomplete)\"\n      seed2_009c_final_eval: 148.34\n      seed2_009c_peak_nve: 1.26\n      seed2_009c_trend: \"peak 359@75K → decline to 148@105K\"\n      seed2_009c_collapse: false\n      protection_robust: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据：009f 被 kill（无完整数据），009c 在 75K 后持续下降至 148（vs baseline 916，仅 16%）。\n      虽然 009c 的 NVE 始终 <1.5x（peak 1.26x@25K），符合 \"no CIVO\" 判定，但绝对性能极差。\n      Worst-tier 解读：dt_embed_dim=0 的 \"保护\" 极不 robust——seed 0 恢复到 503 而 seed 2 跌至 148。\n      保护机制是 seed-dependent 的，008f 不是可靠方案。因果方向（trained dt_emb → CIVO）仍成立\n      （两个 seed 均 NVE<1.5x），但 practical value 有限。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f config cross-seed\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0 (008f)\", \"Seed 2 (009c)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Peak NVE\", \"1.02x@25K\", \"1.26x@25K\"]\n          - [\"Final eval@105K\", \"503\", \"148\"]\n          - [\"Recovery pattern\", \"Zigzag → 503\", \"Peak 359@75K → decline\"]\n          - [\"vs baseline\", \"-45%\", \"-84%\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      009c 的衰退说明去掉 dt_embedding 虽阻止 CIVO 但不保证学习成功——reward prediction\n      退化（MAE 75x baseline）本身就是严重代价。Worst-tier 下，这组数据用于因果论证\n      但不支持任何 practical recommendation。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imag) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"C6 mitigation multi-seed validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 137.0\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_mechanism: \"non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑)\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n      c6_status: \"PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据。s1 成功（95% baseline），s2 在 85-105K 崩溃（715→452→137），但机制与\n      经典 CIVO 不同：s2 是 eval-driven（eval 先跌，value 稳定，entropy ↑），而 008d 是\n      value-driven（value 爆炸，eval 后跌，entropy ↓）。009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定\n      （618→596→836），排除 seed 脆弱性。Worst-tier 解读：dt=1 imagination 未降低\n      collapse rate（与 dt=2 同为 50%），C6 mitigation 被 falsify。Trained dt_embedding\n      通过 Pathway B（non-CIVO policy instability）绕过 dt=1 保护。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 Pathway A vs Pathway B\"\n        headers: [\"Feature\", \"008d s0 (Pathway A: CIVO)\", \"008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B: non-CIVO)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Value change\", \"+130% explosion\", \"+13% stable\"]\n          - [\"Eval change\", \"后跌 -43%\", \"先跌 -81%\"]\n          - [\"NVE driver\", \"Value 分子驱动\", \"Eval 分母驱动\"]\n          - [\"Actor entropy\", \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\", \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\"]\n          - [\"Mechanism\", \"Critic overestimate → actor exploit\", \"Eval crash → value lag\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双 pathway 对比图：value/eval/entropy 三轨并列，008d s0 vs 008e_v3 s2\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 partially falsified 是 worst-tier 最关键的负面结果。论文需重新定位 trained dt_embedding\n      为 \"multi-pathway vulnerability creator\"，而非仅 CIVO trigger。但 Pathway B 机制\n      尚不充分理解——如果 plan_016 显示仅 1/4 崩溃，Pathway B 可能退化为 seed variance。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否为 CIVO 必要条件\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_eval_105K: 204.2\n      nve_range: \"0.39-0.47\"\n      collapse: false\n      collapse_mechanism: \"gradient starvation (actor_loss→0)\"\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n    result_rationale: >\n      实际数据（exp_015b）。Frozen dt_emb 导致 gradient starvation：随机初始化的 dt_embedding\n      不训练，为 RSSM 提供无信息 conditioning→critic 系统性低估（NVE 0.39-0.47x），\n      actor loss 趋近零，学习停滞。eval 在 80-238 间剧烈波动，无稳定收敛。\n      Worst-tier 解读：确认了一个消融点（frozen ≠ trained ≠ absent），但引入新失败模式\n      （gradient starvation），不能作为 mitigation。论文仅能作为 mechanism isolation 证据：\n      dt_emb 的 training 过程本身驱动 CIVO。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Frozen dt_emb 的 gradient starvation 是 worst-tier 下的一个 \"ugly control\"——\n      它证明了 dt_emb training 是 CIVO 必要条件，但方式不够 clean（引入新问题而非\n      neutral baseline）。论文中需小心呈现：这是析因矩阵中的一个消融点，而非独立 finding。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # WALKER WALK — 真正未完成的实验\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"复现 value growth suppression，2 additional seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 460\n        45K: 510\n        55K: 440\n        65K: 550\n        75K: 480\n        85K: 530\n        95K: 520\n        105K: 700\n      seed1_nve_range_55K_105K: [0.60, 0.85]\n      seed1_final_eval: 700\n      seed1_vs_baseline_105K: \"-23.5%\"\n      seed2_eval_trajectory:\n        35K: 420\n        45K: 480\n        55K: 400\n        65K: 470\n        75K: 430\n        85K: 510\n        95K: 490\n        105K: 620\n      seed2_nve_range_55K_105K: [0.55, 0.80]\n      seed2_final_eval: 620\n      seed2_vs_baseline_105K: \"-32.3%\"\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 699\n      cross_seed_nve_mean_105K: 0.63\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 下 C3 在 Walker 内仍 hold，但 variance 更大。Seed 0 (778@105K, 85% baseline)\n      是最优 seed；seed 1-2 预计较低（700/620@105K，76%/68% baseline），因为 subsample OFF +\n      untrained dt_emb 的保护性依赖 RSSM 在 dt=1 数据上的收敛质量——不同 seed 的 RSSM\n      初始化影响 dt=1 prediction 精度，进而影响 value calibration。Normalized v/e 仍一致\n      低于 1.0x（无 CIVO），但绝对性能比 seed 0 差，拉低 cross-seed IQM。\n      在 worst-tier 下这不影响 C3 的定性结论，但 Agarwal et al. (2021) IQM + CI 会更宽。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Eval@105K\", \"778\", \"700\", \"620\", \"699\"]\n          - [\"vs baseline\", \"-15%\", \"-24%\", \"-32%\", \"-24%\"]\n          - [\"NVE@105K\", \"0.59x\", \"0.65x\", \"0.72x\", \"0.65x\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"No\", \"No\", \"No\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed 学习曲线叠加，均显示 zigzag 但幅度和收敛点不同\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 在 Walker 内 robust（3/3 seeds NVE<1.0x，无崩溃），但跨 seed 绝对性能变化大\n      （620-778，22% 跨距）。Worst-tier 下，这组数据仅 reinforces Walker-specific 结论。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"缩窄 Pathway B collapse probability estimate\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 830\n      seed3_nve_105K: 0.78\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed4_eval_105K: 790\n      seed4_nve_105K: 0.82\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      total_collapse_rate: \"1/4 (25%)\"\n      pathway_b_interpretation: \"closer to seed variance than systematic pathway\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 核心假设之一：\"Pathway B control experiment reveals 008e_v3_s2 collapse\n      was closer to random seed variance than a systematic second pathway\"。Seed 3-4\n      均不崩溃，collapse rate 从 1/2 降至 1/4（25%）。在 4 个 seed 中仅 1 个崩溃，\n      且该崩溃的机制签名（entropy ↑, eval-driven）与 CIVO 不同，更接近 policy\n      optimization 的随机脆弱性。这削弱 \"multiple vulnerability pathways\" 叙事——\n      Pathway B 不是 systematic mechanism 而是 seed-specific instability。\n      论文需要 honest reporting：trained dt_emb + dt=1 imag 的 collapse rate ~25%，\n      无法确定是否显著高于 baseline（baseline 0/2 seeds 崩溃，但 n 太小无法做统计检验）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 all seeds\"\n        headers: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE@105K\", \"Collapse?\", \"Mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed 1 (s1)\", \"869.9\", \"0.80x\", \"No\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"Seed 2 (s2)\", \"137.0\", \"3.78x\", \"Yes\", \"Eval-driven (Pathway B)\"]\n          - [\"Seed 3 (pred)\", \"830\", \"0.78x\", \"No\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"Seed 4 (pred)\", \"790\", \"0.82x\", \"No\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed 学习曲线 + NVE 轨迹，标注 seed 2 崩溃点及与其余 3 seeds 的分歧\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/4 collapse rate 在 worst-tier 下严重削弱 Pathway B 论述。论文可能需要从\n      \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\" 退回到\n      \"trained dt_embedding reliably triggers CIVO (Pathway A, blocked by dt=1 imag);\n      rare policy instability events (1/4 seeds) may or may not be related\"。\n      这实际上部分 salvages dt=1 mitigation（3/4 seeds 成功，接近 baseline），\n      但 honest reporting 要求承认 n=4 统计力量不足。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"不同 NVE 阈值的分类精度，0 GPU 成本\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_only:\n        threshold_1_3x:\n          accuracy: 0.80\n          sensitivity: 1.0\n          specificity: 0.50\n          note: \"1 FP (009c@25K NVE=1.26 borderline, 但 35K+ 限定后为 TN)\"\n        threshold_1_5x:\n          accuracy: 1.0\n          sensitivity: 1.0\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"4/4 perfect at 35K+\"\n        threshold_1_7x:\n          accuracy: 0.80\n          sensitivity: 0.67\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"009b peak NVE=1.62x barely above 1.7x? Actually no, 1.62<1.7 → FN\"\n        threshold_2_0x:\n          accuracy: 0.80\n          sensitivity: 0.67\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"009b peak 2.05x@25K excluded by 35K+ rule; 1.62x@45K<2.0 → FN\"\n        auroc: 0.98\n      cross_env_walker_cheetah:\n        threshold_1_5x:\n          accuracy: 0.64\n          sensitivity: 0.40\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"Walker 2/2 trained→TP; Cheetah 0/3 trained→FN; all untrained→TN\"\n        auroc: 0.72\n      cross_env_all_three:\n        threshold_1_5x:\n          accuracy: 0.58\n          sensitivity: 0.29\n          specificity: 1.0\n          note: \"仅 Walker 2/7 trained seeds 被检出\"\n        auroc: 0.65\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 内 1.5x threshold 完美分离（AUROC~0.98），这是 existing data 的强结论。\n      但在 worst-tier 下，Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb seeds NVE 全部 <1.5x（范围 0.8-1.4x），\n      因为 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity characteristics 不同——reward density 更高、state\n      dynamics 更 smooth，dt_emb 的 observation decoder 梯度不产生同样的 systematic bias。\n      这导致 threshold 在 Cheetah 上产生大量 false negatives（degradation 发生但 NVE\n      不超标）。Cross-env AUROC 从 0.98 降至 ~0.72，远低于 diagnostic tool 的实用标准。\n      论文必须 honest report：\"NVE>1.5x is a reliable Walker Walk diagnostic but does NOT\n      generalize to Cheetah Run, where degradation manifests through different dynamics.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NVE 1.5x threshold cross-environment performance\"\n        headers: [\"Environment\", \"Trained Seeds\", \"TP\", \"FN\", \"Untrained Seeds\", \"TN\", \"FP\", \"Accuracy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3\", \"3\", \"0\", \"2\", \"2\", \"0\", \"5/5=1.00\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3\", \"3\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3/6=0.50\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3\", \"3\", \"3\", \"0\", \"3/6=0.50\"]\n          - [\"Cross-env total\", \"9\", \"3\", \"6\", \"8\", \"8\", \"0\", \"11/17=0.65\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC 曲线：Walker-only (AUROC=0.98) vs cross-env (AUROC=0.72)\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE 方法论是 worst-tier 下论文的 second contribution pillar，但必须诚实定位为\n      \"validated in Walker Walk, proposed for broader adoption with caveats\"。跨环境失败\n      不否定方法论本身——而是揭示 CIVO 机制的 environment-specificity。论文应讨论\n      为何 Cheetah 的 NVE pattern 不同（reward density、RSSM fidelity characteristics），\n      将 negative result 转化为 diagnostic insight。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CHEETAH RUN — 跨环境泛化（worst-tier 核心失败区域）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"第二 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_final_eval: 849.8\n      seed1_status: \"DONE (exp_010a)\"\n      seed2_final_eval: 825\n      seed3_final_eval: 862\n      cross_seed_mean: 846\n      cross_seed_std: 19\n      ve_ratio_stable: \"0.65-0.72 from 135K+\"\n      ve_ratio_trajectory:\n        25K: 0.09\n        35K: 0.19\n        45K: 0.28\n        55K: 0.36\n        65K: 0.47\n        75K: 0.57\n        85K: 0.63\n        95K: 0.66\n        105K: 0.68\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 在 DreamerV3 上训练正常，peak ~850。Seed 1 已完成（849.8）。\n      Cheetah 的 reward 是 forward velocity（dense, smooth），收敛特性与 Walker Walk 类似\n      但 v/e trajectory 略低（Cheetah 的 discount structure 和 reward scale 不同）。\n      Baseline 本身不受 worst-tier 影响——环境正常运行是所有后续实验的前提。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 确立 Cheetah Run 的参考线。v/e calibration（~0.68@105K）与 Walker（~0.656@105K）\n      高度一致，为 NVE 比较提供合理基础。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"复现 CIVO collapse in Cheetah — worst-tier 预测失败\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          5K: 31\n          15K: 190\n          25K: 370\n          35K: 520\n          45K: 490\n          55K: 440\n          65K: 400\n          75K: 380\n          85K: 360\n          95K: 370\n          105K: 385\n        value_trajectory:\n          25K: 28\n          35K: 85\n          45K: 120\n          55K: 140\n          65K: 145\n          75K: 140\n          85K: 130\n          95K: 125\n          105K: 128\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.94\n          45K: 0.92\n          55K: 0.95\n          65K: 0.83\n          75K: 0.72\n          85K: 0.68\n          95K: 0.65\n          105K: 0.63\n        collapse: false\n        peak_nve: 0.95\n        pattern: \"gradual decline without value acceleration\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 480\n          45K: 430\n          55K: 380\n          65K: 350\n          75K: 340\n          85K: 360\n          95K: 375\n          105K: 390\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 1.25\n          45K: 1.30\n          55K: 1.28\n          65K: 1.15\n          75K: 0.98\n          85K: 0.92\n          95K: 0.88\n          105K: 0.85\n        collapse: false\n        peak_nve: 1.30\n        pattern: \"mild overestimation plateau then decline — not accelerating\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 550\n          45K: 520\n          55K: 470\n          65K: 430\n          75K: 410\n          85K: 420\n          95K: 430\n          105K: 445\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.82\n          45K: 0.85\n          55K: 0.90\n          65K: 0.87\n          75K: 0.80\n          85K: 0.78\n          95K: 0.75\n          105K: 0.74\n        collapse: false\n        peak_nve: 0.90\n        pattern: \"value suppression — similar to Walker dt=4\"\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_nve_max: 1.30\n      cross_seed_nve_mean_at_55K: 1.04\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 407\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-52%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 核心假设：\"Cheetah Run shows performance degradation with dt>1 but NVE pattern\n      differs\"。三个 seed 均显示 degradation（eval 407 平均 vs baseline 846，-52%），但\n      NVE 模式与 Walker 定性不同：\n      (1) Seed 0 (NVE 0.63-0.95x)：value suppression 模式，类似 Walker dt=4——RSSM 在\n          Cheetah 的 dt>1 prediction 质量差导致 critic underestimate 而非 overestimate。\n          Cheetah 的 velocity-based reward 结构使 dt>1 reward prediction 偏差方向不同。\n      (2) Seed 1 (NVE peak 1.30x)：温和过估计但不加速。NVE 在 35-55K 达到 1.25-1.30x\n          后自行下降至 0.85x。与 Walker 008d 的加速发散（1.71x→2.09x→4.12x）形成鲜明对比。\n          Cheetah 的 RSSM 可能在 dt>1 有更好的 self-correction 能力（state space 更规则）。\n      (3) Seed 2 (NVE 0.74-0.90x)：纯 value suppression。\n      没有任何 seed 的 NVE 超过 1.5x → 1.5x threshold 在 Cheetah 上完全失效（0/3 detected）。\n      Degradation 确实存在但不是 CIVO——更可能是 learning signal reduction (C5) + RSSM\n      fidelity gap 的混合效应，不伴随 positive feedback loop。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed NVE\"\n        headers: [\"Step\", \"Seed 0 NVE\", \"Seed 1 NVE\", \"Seed 2 NVE\", \"Walker 008d NVE (ref)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.94\", \"1.25\", \"0.82\", \"1.71\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"0.92\", \"1.30\", \"0.85\", \"2.09\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"0.95\", \"1.28\", \"0.90\", \"4.12\"]\n          - [\"65K\", \"0.83\", \"1.15\", \"0.87\", \"(collapsed)\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"0.63\", \"0.85\", \"0.74\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah vs Walker NVE 轨迹对比：Walker 加速发散 vs Cheetah 平稳/下降\"\n      - \"Cheetah 3-seed eval 曲线 + baseline reference\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst-tier 的 defining result。Degradation 存在但 CIVO 缺失。论文必须承认：\n      \"The CIVO mechanism (accelerating NVE feedback loop) is environment-specific. In Cheetah\n      Run, trained dt_embedding degrades performance through a different mechanism — likely\n      learning signal quality degradation without the positive feedback loop observed in Walker.\"\n      Limitations section 需讨论 Cheetah 为何不同：(a) reward 结构（pure velocity vs\n      complex locomotion reward），(b) state space dimensionality 和 smoothness，\n      (c) RSSM 对不同 dynamics 的 fidelity characteristics。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Cheetah 因果控制——worst-tier 预测无 clean separation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 470\n          55K: 400\n          75K: 370\n          105K: 410\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.75\n          55K: 0.90\n          75K: 0.85\n          105K: 0.70\n        pattern: \"similar degradation to trained dt_emb\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 510\n          55K: 430\n          75K: 400\n          105K: 440\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.68\n          55K: 0.80\n          75K: 0.75\n          105K: 0.65\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 490\n          55K: 420\n          75K: 380\n          105K: 380\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 1.10\n          55K: 1.05\n          75K: 0.90\n          105K: 0.82\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 410\n      cross_seed_nve_range: [0.65, 1.10]\n      nve_overlap_with_trained: \"substantial (trained range [0.63, 1.30] vs untrained [0.65, 1.10])\"\n      vs_trained_dt_emb_eval_diff: \"+0.7% (not significant)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 假设：\"NVE 1.5x threshold doesn't separate trained/untrained in Cheetah\"。\n      去掉 dt_embedding 后 Cheetah 的 eval 和 NVE 与 trained dt_emb 配置几乎无差异\n      （eval 410 vs 407, NVE 0.65-1.10 vs 0.63-1.30）。原因：Cheetah 的 degradation\n      根源是 learning signal reduction（subsample ON 导致有效 transition 数减半）而非\n      dt_embedding-driven CIVO。在 Walker 中，去掉 dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO feedback loop，\n      产生 dramatic 差异（008f NVE<1.0 vs 008d NVE>2.0）；在 Cheetah 中，没有\n      CIVO feedback loop 需要阻止，所以去掉 dt_emb 不产生 significant effect。\n      这是 worst-tier 下最难处理的结果——直接否定 C2 因果链在 Cheetah 上的适用性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah: trained vs no dt_emb\"\n        headers: [\"Metric\", \"Trained dt_emb (plan_021)\", \"No dt_emb (plan_022)\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Eval mean@105K\", \"407\", \"410\", \"+0.7% (ns)\"]\n          - [\"NVE range (35K+)\", \"[0.63, 1.30]\", \"[0.65, 1.10]\", \"overlapping\"]\n          - [\"Collapse rate\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"identical\"]\n          - [\"NVE>1.5x rate\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"identical\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained vs untrained dt_emb: eval + NVE 并排对比，标注 overlap region\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 \"no separation\" 是 worst-tier 最 damaging 的 cross-env negative result。\n      论文需要解释为什么 Walker 的因果机制不 transfer：dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 的\n      observation decoder 梯度路径可能不产生同向 systematic bias，因为 Cheetah 的\n      state space structure（关节速度为主导 observable）让 RSSM 对 dt>1 的 prediction\n      error 分布更 uniform（不集中在特定 decoder head），无法形成 amplification loop。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Cheetah value growth suppression — worst-tier 预测无 clear advantage\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 490\n          55K: 430\n          75K: 450\n          105K: 520\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.80\n          55K: 0.75\n          75K: 0.70\n          105K: 0.65\n      seed1:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 520\n          55K: 460\n          75K: 480\n          105K: 550\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.72\n          55K: 0.78\n          75K: 0.68\n          105K: 0.60\n      seed2:\n        eval_trajectory:\n          35K: 480\n          55K: 440\n          75K: 430\n          105K: 490\n        nve_trajectory:\n          35K: 0.85\n          55K: 0.82\n          75K: 0.75\n          105K: 0.70\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_105K: 520\n      vs_baseline: \"-39%\"\n      vs_trained_dt_emb: \"+28% (520 vs 407)\"\n      vs_no_dt_emb: \"+27% (520 vs 410)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Subsample OFF 保留完整 learning signal，所以 eval 高于 plan_021/022（520 vs 407/410）。\n      但这个提升来自 learning signal preservation（C5），不是 value suppression（C3）。\n      NVE 在 0.60-0.85x 范围，与 plan_022 (0.65-1.10) 有 overlap。Worst-tier 解读：\n      C3 在 Cheetah 上不能 cleanly 验证，因为 baseline comparison 被 subsample 差异混淆。\n      To isolate C3 需要 subsample ON + untrained dt_emb（但 Walker 已有 008c/008e_v3\n      数据做此对比）。在 Cheetah 上，所有 dt>1 配置都 degrades，无论 dt_emb 状态如何。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah untrained dt_emb 的 eval 提升主要归因于 subsample OFF（保留学习信号），\n      非 value suppression 机制。C3 声明在 Cheetah 上 confounded。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CARTPOLE SWINGUP — 第三环境（worst-tier 同样失败）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"非 locomotion 环境 baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_final_eval: 840\n      seed1_final_eval: 820\n      seed2_final_eval: 855\n      cross_seed_mean: 838\n      ve_ratio_stable: \"0.60-0.68 from 135K+\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DreamerV3 上的 well-solved benchmark，baseline ~840。\n      V/e ratio 收敛到 ~0.64，略低于 Walker/Cheetah，因为 Cartpole 的 sparse initial\n      reward（swingup 前 reward 极低）使 value function 在 early training 更保守。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常。Cartpole 的 non-locomotion dynamics（pendulum + cart）\n      为跨环境泛化测试提供了不同 task family。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"复现 CIVO collapse in Cartpole — worst-tier 预测 no CIVO\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0:\n        eval_105K: 320\n        peak_nve: 0.75\n        pattern: \"value suppression — critic under-estimates\"\n      seed1:\n        eval_105K: 280\n        peak_nve: 0.90\n        pattern: \"learning failure — low asymptote\"\n      seed2:\n        eval_105K: 350\n        peak_nve: 0.65\n        pattern: \"value suppression\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 317\n      vs_baseline: \"-62%\"\n      collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n      nve_max: 0.90\n      nve_gt_1_5x: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 的 sparse reward structure 使 dt>1 transitions 的 reward prediction\n      几乎无信息（swingup 前大量 near-zero reward）。Trained dt_emb 不会产生 CIVO 因为：\n      (1) RSSM 对 dt>1 的 reward prediction 偏差方向是 under-estimation（sparse reward\n          的高 reward events 在 dt>1 步后更难预测，导致 systematic negative bias）；\n      (2) Observation decoder 梯度集中在 pendulum angle 上（单一关键 observable），\n          不像 Walker 的 multi-head gradient（orientations/velocity/height）能形成\n          amplification；\n      (3) Cartpole 的 state space（4D: cart pos/vel + pole angle/vel）远小于\n          Walker（24D+），RSSM 的 dt>1 fidelity gap 更小。\n      结果是 degradation 但以 value suppression/learning failure 形式出现，无 CIVO signature。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole trained dt_emb NVE\"\n        headers: [\"Seed\", \"Peak NVE\", \"NVE@105K\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0\", \"0.75\", \"0.60\", \"No\", \"Value suppression\"]\n          - [\"1\", \"0.90\", \"0.70\", \"No\", \"Learning failure\"]\n          - [\"2\", \"0.65\", \"0.55\", \"No\", \"Value suppression\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的 NVE pattern（全部 <1.0x）与 Walker 的 CIVO（>1.5x accelerating）和\n      Cheetah 的 mixed pattern（0.6-1.3x stable）都不同。三个环境三种 failure mode：\n      Walker=CIVO, Cheetah=mild overestimation/plateau, Cartpole=value suppression。\n      这证明 dt>1 degradation 是 universal 但 mechanism 是 environment-specific。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Cartpole 因果控制\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 310\n      seed1_eval_105K: 290\n      seed2_eval_105K: 340\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 313\n      vs_trained_dt_emb: \"-1.3% (not significant)\"\n      nve_range: [0.55, 0.85]\n      nve_overlap_with_trained: \"complete overlap\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 类似，去掉 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 上不产生 significant 差异。\n      Degradation 根源是 learning signal reduction（C5），dt_emb 不是 primary factor。\n      Eval 313 vs trained 317，差异在噪声范围内。NVE 完全 overlap。\n      Walker 中 008f vs 008d 的 dramatic 差异（NVE 0.97x vs 2.09x）在 Cartpole\n      不可复现——因为 Cartpole 没有 CIVO feedback loop 需要 dt_emb 来 trigger。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的 \"no separation\" 进一步确认：CIVO 是 Walker-specific phenomenon。\n      Cross-env data 现在显示 3 environments 中仅 1 个有 CIVO。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 分析类实验（0 GPU 或低 GPU）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment-specific characteristics\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 10.2\n        dt2_obs_mse: 18.5\n        obs_gap: 1.81\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.008\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.012\n        reward_gap: 1.50\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 15.8\n        dt2_obs_mse: 22.3\n        obs_gap: 1.41\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.035\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.065\n        reward_gap: 1.86\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n        dt1_obs_mse: 9.5\n        dt2_obs_mse: 19.8\n        obs_gap: 2.08\n        dt1_reward_mae: 0.52\n        dt2_reward_mae: 0.54\n        reward_gap: 1.04\n      walker_vs_cheetah_obs_gap_comparison:\n        walker_baseline: 2.04\n        cheetah_baseline: 1.81\n        walker_trained: 1.30\n        cheetah_trained: 1.41\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 与 Walker 数值接近但分布不同。关键差异：\n      (1) Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb reward gap (1.86x) 低于 Walker (2.78x)——\n          Cheetah 的 velocity reward 更 smooth，dt_emb 不会像 Walker 那样在 reward head\n          产生 large systematic bias。但注意 Walker 的 reward gradient = 0（by architecture），\n          所以 reward gap 不是 CIVO 的直接驱动因素。\n      (2) Cheetah 的 obs_gap (1.81x baseline, 1.41x trained) 与 Walker (2.04x, 1.30x) \n          类似，但 obs MSE 的绝对值更低——Cheetah 的 state space 更规则，RSSM 建模质量更好。\n      (3) Cheetah trained dt_emb 的 dt1 abs obs_MSE (15.8) 显著低于 Walker (41.31)——\n          模型没有像 Walker 那样因为 CIVO 而全面崩塌。\n      Worst-tier 解读：fidelity gap 存在但不 sufficient to trigger CIVO in Cheetah。\n      机制的 environment-specificity 体现在 fidelity gap 如何通过 gradient pathways\n      传播到 value function——Walker 的 multi-head gradient structure 放大 bias，\n      Cheetah 的更 uniform gradient 不放大。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment RSSM fidelity comparison\"\n        headers: [\"Model\", \"Env\", \"dt1 obs_MSE\", \"dt2 obs_MSE\", \"obs gap\", \"reward gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"Walker\", \"13.49\", \"27.50\", \"2.04x\", \"1.56x\"]\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"Cheetah\", \"10.2\", \"18.5\", \"1.81x\", \"1.50x\"]\n          - [\"Trained dt_emb\", \"Walker\", \"41.31\", \"53.67\", \"1.30x\", \"2.78x\"]\n          - [\"Trained dt_emb\", \"Cheetah\", \"15.8\", \"22.3\", \"1.41x\", \"1.86x\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb\", \"Walker\", \"8.01\", \"22.04\", \"2.75x\", \"1.01x\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb\", \"Cheetah\", \"9.5\", \"19.8\", \"2.08x\", \"1.04x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-env RSSM fidelity heatmap: obs_MSE × reward_MAE 四象限，标注 CIVO/non-CIVO regions\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity gap 是 necessary but not sufficient for CIVO。Cheetah 有 gap 但\n      无 CIVO 放大。论文需讨论 gradient pathway structure 作为 missing mediator。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Walker + Cheetah actor entropy trajectory 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_civo_collapsed_008d:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"8.2→-1.9→-3.5→-4.6→-4.9\"\n        pattern: \"entropy ↓: policy becomes deterministic during CIVO\"\n      walker_pathway_b_008e_v3_s2:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-5.1→-5.2→-5.2→-4.5→-3.8\"\n        pattern: \"entropy ↑: policy destabilizes (opposite of CIVO)\"\n      walker_healthy_008a:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-4.2→-4.5→-4.6→-4.7→-4.8\"\n        pattern: \"entropy stable: normal policy convergence\"\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-3.8→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2→-4.3\"\n        pattern: \"entropy stable: no CIVO or Pathway B signature\"\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb:\n        entropy_trajectory: \"-3.7→-3.9→-4.0→-4.1→-4.2\"\n        pattern: \"entropy stable: indistinguishable from trained\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy 在 Walker 中是 CIVO 和 Pathway B 的 discriminating signature：\n      CIVO → entropy ↓（critic overestimate 让 actor converge to exploitative policy），\n      Pathway B → entropy ↑（policy destabilization，actor 失去 coherent strategy）。\n      在 Cheetah 中，因为没有 CIVO 或 Pathway B，所有配置的 entropy trajectory \n      几乎一致（stable decline），无法作为 diagnostic tool。这进一步确认 Cheetah 的\n      degradation 机制不同——没有 actor 层面的 pathological dynamics。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Walker entropy 三轨对比（CIVO↓ / Pathway B↑ / healthy→）vs Cheetah 无差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy analysis 在 Walker 内是有力 diagnostic，但在 Cheetah 上无差异性。\n      论文可呈现为 Walker-specific finding。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"V(s) vs MC return 分布分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_divergence:\n        value_mean: 97.5\n        mc_return_mean: 35\n        ks_statistic: 0.72\n        pattern: \"right-shifted value distribution — systematic overestimation\"\n      walker_008a_calibration:\n        value_mean: 280\n        mc_return_mean: 550\n        ks_statistic: 0.35\n        pattern: \"left-shifted but not pathological — conservative value\"\n      cheetah_trained_divergence:\n        value_mean: 140\n        mc_return_mean: 180\n        ks_statistic: 0.28\n        pattern: \"mild underestimation — no systematic overestimation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 008d 的 V(s) 分布系统性右偏（overestimate），与 MC return 严重脱节\n      （KS=0.72）。这是 CIVO 的 direct evidence。Cheetah trained dt_emb 的 V(s)\n      分布仅轻微左偏（underestimate, KS=0.28），不存在 systematic overestimation。\n      Worst-tier 下，分布分析强化了 \"CIVO is Walker-specific\" 的结论。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"V(s) vs MC return 散点图 + violin plot: Walker 008d (divergent) vs Cheetah (aligned)\"\n    analysis: >\n      分布分析是比 v/e ratio 更 informative 的 proxy，但在 worst-tier 下仅确认\n      已知结论。投入 1 GPU-hour 的 ROI 有限。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"learned dt_emb vectors 的 dt=1 vs dt=2 similarity evolution\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_initial_cosine: 0.85\n      walker_trained_30K_cosine: 0.42\n      walker_trained_60K_cosine: 0.28\n      walker_trend: \"diverging — dt=1 and dt=2 embeddings become increasingly dissimilar\"\n      cheetah_initial_cosine: 0.85\n      cheetah_trained_30K_cosine: 0.55\n      cheetah_trained_60K_cosine: 0.48\n      cheetah_trend: \"partial divergence — less separation than Walker\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 中 dt_emb 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 vectors 快速分化（cosine 0.85→0.28），\n      说明 network 积极利用 dt conditioning 来做 specialized predictions——这是\n      CIVO 的前提条件。Cheetah 中分化较缓（0.85→0.48），说明 dt_emb 被利用程度\n      较低——network 未充分 specialize on dt information，因此不会形成 strong\n      dt-dependent value bias。这与 Cheetah 的 observation decoder 梯度更 uniform\n      的假设一致——没有足够的 gradient signal 来 push dt_emb 向 high-separation direction。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"dt_emb cosine similarity vs training step: Walker (fast divergence) vs Cheetah (slow)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine analysis 提供了为什么 CIVO 在 Cheetah 不发生的 additional mechanistic insight：\n      dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中学到的 dt 区分度更低，减少了 condition-dependent bias 的\n      severity。可作为 Discussion section 的 supporting analysis。0 GPU cost，值得做。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # EXPLORATORY / MITIGATION\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"RSSM 不确定性门控 imagination 截断——Walker Walk pilot\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 540\n      vs_baseline: \"-41%\"\n      nve_peak: 1.15\n      collapse: false\n      truncation_rate_at_dt2: 0.35\n      effective_horizon_mean: 11.2\n      issues:\n        - \"RSSM ensemble disagreement 校准不准——在 dt=1 transitions 上也频繁触发截断\"\n        - \"有效 horizon 从 15 降至 ~11，减少了 long-range credit assignment\"\n        - \"稳定但性能远低于 008e_v3 seed 1 (870) 和 baseline (916)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RSSM 本身不提供 well-calibrated uncertainty estimates（DreamerV3 使用 single RSSM，\n      不是 ensemble）。Pilot 需要额外实现 RSSM ensemble 或使用 KL divergence as proxy。\n      在 worst-tier 下，uncertainty estimate 噪声大：dt=1 transitions 的不确定性\n      也偶尔偏高（false truncation），而 dt>1 transitions 的不确定性不总是偏高\n      （missed truncation）。Net effect: truncation 防止了最严重的 collapse（NVE 不超 1.5x），\n      但 over-truncation 缩短有效 horizon，损失 long-range learning signal。\n      Eval 540 好于 008d collapse (83) 但远低于 008e_v3 success (870)。\n      不适合作为 paper contribution——implementation complexity 高但 benefit 有限。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Uncertainty truncation 是 \"reasonable but noisy\" 的 mitigation。在 worst-tier 下\n      不足以写入论文——更适合 future work section 的 one-sentence mention。\n      CoRL deadline 前不值得投入更多 GPU。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"第三 DMC locomotion 环境——worst-tier 预测：P2 优先级，可能不跑\"\n    expected_results:\n      likely_status: \"NOT RUN before CoRL deadline (P2 priority)\"\n      if_run:\n        baseline_mean: 250\n        trained_dt_emb_mean: 120\n        trained_dt_emb_nve_pattern: \"mixed — some seeds >1.0x, none >1.5x\"\n        no_dt_emb_mean: 130\n        separation: \"minimal\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 sparse reward + contact-rich dynamics，DreamerV3 baseline 仅 ~250\n      （远低于 Walker/Cheetah）。在 worst-tier 下，即使跑了，低 baseline 性能使得\n      v/e ratio 极不稳定（分母小），NVE 信噪比差，无法得出 clean 结论。\n      此外，45 GPU-hours 的预算在 13 天 deadline 前不值得投入——这些资源应用于\n      确保 Walker 数据的 presentation quality。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      P2 实验在 worst-tier 下应果断放弃。论文不需要第三个 negative result\n      来说明 CIVO 是 environment-specific。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CROSS-CUTTING ANALYSIS\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Full cross-environment summary table\"\n    plan_id: \"N/A (synthesis)\"\n    description: \"综合所有环境的 CIVO 检测结果\"\n    expected_results:\n      environments_with_confirmed_civo: 1\n      walker_walk:\n        civo_confirmed: true\n        nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: \"3/3 (100%)\"\n        collapse_rate: \"1/2 to 2/3 seeds\"\n        full_sgs_nve: 1.00\n        mechanism: \"observation-decoder-driven gradient amplification\"\n      cheetah_run:\n        civo_confirmed: false\n        nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: \"0/3 (0%)\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        degradation: \"yes (-52% baseline)\"\n        mechanism: \"learning signal reduction + mild fidelity gap, no positive feedback loop\"\n      cartpole_swingup:\n        civo_confirmed: false\n        nve_gt_1_5x_sensitivity: \"0/3 (0%)\"\n        collapse_rate: \"0/3\"\n        degradation: \"yes (-62% baseline)\"\n        mechanism: \"value suppression from sparse reward + dt>1 prediction noise\"\n      cross_env_threshold_accuracy: 0.65\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-tier 的 defining outcome：只有 Walker Walk 确认 CIVO。Cheetah 和 Cartpole\n      都显示 dt>1 degradation 但通过不同机制。1.5x NVE threshold 在 Walker 内完美\n      但跨环境仅 0.65 accuracy。这迫使论文完全退守 single-environment depth story。\n      贡献变为：(1) Walker Walk 的 rigorous factorial diagnosis，(2) NVE methodology\n      （validated in Walker, proposed with caveats），(3) gradient-level evidence\n      （Full-SGS），(4) TAWM contrast（MPC vs imagination）。\n      Drop 所有 \"general architectural vulnerability\" 语言。\n      Add extensive limitations section 讨论 environment-specificity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment CIVO summary\"\n        headers: [\"Environment\", \"Degradation?\", \"CIVO (NVE>1.5x)?\", \"Collapse?\", \"Mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"Yes (-5% to -85%)\", \"Yes (3/3 seeds)\", \"Yes (1-2/3)\", \"CIVO + Pathway B\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"Yes (-52%)\", \"No (0/3 seeds)\", \"No (0/3)\", \"Learning signal + fidelity gap\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"Yes (-62%)\", \"No (0/3 seeds)\", \"No (0/3)\", \"Value suppression\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-env NVE distribution violin plot: Walker (wide, right-skewed >1.5x) vs Cheetah/Cartpole (narrow, centered <1.0x)\"\n    analysis: >\n      论文 framing 最终版：\n      \"We provide the first rigorous factorial diagnosis of why temporal abstraction fails\n      in DreamerV3's imagination-based training, demonstrated in Walker Walk with controlled\n      design. The CIVO mechanism — trained dt-embedding amplifying RSSM fidelity gaps into\n      value overestimation through observation decoder gradients — is confirmed by gradient-level\n      intervention (Full-SGS). Our NVE diagnostic methodology achieves perfect separation\n      in Walker Walk but does not generalize to Cheetah Run or Cartpole Swingup, where\n      degradation proceeds through different mechanisms. This environment-specificity itself\n      is an important finding: temporal abstraction fails universally in our experiments,\n      but the failure mode is environment-dependent, complicating one-size-fits-all solutions.\n      The contrast with TAWM (Nhu et al., ICML 2025), where dt-conditioning succeeds in MPC\n      but fails in imagination, remains the paper's strongest novelty claim regardless of\n      cross-environment generalization.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"feed3564-d2fd-471f-ba3e-2644a7a39578","total_cost_usd":1.08058325,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41539,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":31161,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41539,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":31161,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41539},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":36096,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.036206,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":31161,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41539,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0443772500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8b157116-4748-4726-9c93-9c66b59735e8"}
